        {
          "id": "841147f5-48c7-3c6e-ab4a-d90a91082013",
          "content": {
            "id": "841147f5-48c7-3c6e-ab4a-d90a91082013",
            "contentType": "VIDEO",
            "title": "NorthWestern Energy & Black Hills to merge, Caterpillar upgrade",
            "description": "<p>Here are some of the stories Wall Street is watching on Tuesday, Aug. 19.</p>\n<p>NorthWestern Energy (<a data-i13n=\"cpos:1;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/quote/NWE\">NWE</a>) and Black Hills (<a data-i13n=\"cpos:2;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/quote/BKH\">BKH</a>) have agreed to merge, with the companies having a combined enterprise value of $15.4 billion.</p>\n<p>Shares of Fabrinet (<a data-i13n=\"cpos:3;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/quote/FN\">FN</a>) are sliding despite posting Q4 results that topped estimates.</p>\n<p>Caterpillar (<a data-i13n=\"cpos:4;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/quote/CAT\">CAT</a>) shares were upgraded to Outperform from In Line at Evercore ISI.</p>\n<p>Stay up to date on the latest market action, minute-by-minute, with <a data-i13n=\"cpos:5;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/videos/series/market-minute/\">Yahoo Finance's Market Minute.</a></p>",
